    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θθ</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆτα</span></b> , τό, indecl.,
		ninth (later eighth) letter of the Gr. alphabet: as numeral <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ᾽</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννέα, ἔνατος</span>
			, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
				q'
			</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				000
			</span></i>: abbreviation for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span>
			(or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέθανε, τέθνηκε,
			θανατωτέον</span>) found in certain Ptolemaic Mss. of <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(1).612
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pers.
				4.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mart.
				7.37
			</span></i>, Wessely <i>Schrifttaf. zur
				ält.lat.Paläogr.</i>No.<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFay.</u>
				105 iii 26
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, Dessau <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Lat.Sel.</u>
				5140
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆτα</span>
			.</div>
